# CMake and tests

## Module sources

Every new implementation `.cpp` must be added to that module’s own `CMakeLists.txt` (`engine/<module>/CMakeLists.txt` or `games/arkanoid/<sim|app>/CMakeLists.txt`). Omitting it means the file never compiles.

Executable is `arkanoid` (`games/arkanoid/main.cpp`); it links `arkanoid_app` and `sgl_sfml`. Only `sgl_sfml` (and the executable via that link) links SFML. `arkanoid_sim` and `arkanoid_app` stay SFML-free at the include level.

## Tests (Debug only)

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

- Unit tests: `tests/engine/` and `tests/arkanoid/`; GoogleTest 1.18 via FetchContent
- Register with `add_unit_test(...)` in the leaf `CMakeLists.txt`
- Prefer tests that do not open a window; `event_translate_test` links `SFML::Window` but opens none
- Fixture names like `*Should` when adding behavioral suites

When changing a module, update or add unit tests under the matching `tests/engine/<module>/` or `tests/arkanoid/<sim|app>/` leaf.
